    "last_reason": "stop",
    "final_answer": "Upgraded `settlement_reconcile.py` from v1 to v2 and verified it against the live v2 server.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Switched the endpoint from `/v1/graphql` to `/v2/graphql`.\n- Replaced the single `settlements` query with the paginated v2 connection:\n  - `settlements(first: 100, after: $after)`\n  - reads `nodes` and `pageInfo { endCursor hasNextPage }`\n- Follows `hasNextPage` rather than treating short or empty pages as the end.\n- Deduplicates by `id`, keeping the last version received, so amended settlements are written exactly once.\n- Retries `429 Too Many Requests` using `Retry-After` and resends the identical request, including the same `after` cursor.\n- Restarts the traversal from the beginning, without `after`, if the server rejects a cursor as malformed or expired.\n- Writes output only after a complete traversal, avoiding partial reconciliation files.\n\n## Verification\n\nAgainst `http://the VM's public address:18081`:\n\n- Traversed **27 pages**\n- Reconciled **1,873 settlements**, all with unique IDs\n- Handled **19 duplicate/amended deliveries**, **4 empty pages**, and **9 short pages**\n- Encountered and retried a real `429`\n- Compared with v1: **0 missing**, **0 extra**, **0 value mismatches**\n\nAlso tested the error paths with a local mock server: cursor-expiry restart, `429` retry, empty page, amendment replacement \u2014 all passed.",
